{"info": {"total": 224, "parameters": {"skip": 0, "limit": 8, "q": "landscape", "cc0": "1", "culture": "China", "has_image": "1", "select": "accession_number,accession_number_sortable,cover_accession_number,department,gallery,classification_type,department,collection", "search": "landscape"}}, "data": [{"id": 142642, "accession_number": "1966.367", "share_license_status": "CC0", "tombstone": "Spring Landscape (\u6625\u666f\u5716), 1666. Kuncan (Chinese, 1612\u2013c. 1673). Double album leaf mounted as a handscroll; ink and color on paper; overall: 31.8 x 64.5 cm (12 1/2 x 25 3/8 in.). The Cleveland Museum of Art, Purchase from the J. H. Wade Fund, 1966.367", "current_location": null, "title": "Spring Landscape", "title_in_original_language": "\u6625\u666f\u5716", "creation_date": "1666", "creation_date_earliest": 1666, "creation_date_latest": 1666, "artists_tags": ["male"], "culture": ["China, Qing dynasty (1644\u20131911)"], "technique": "double album leaf mounted as a handscroll; ink and color on paper", "support_materials": [], "department": "Chinese Art", "collection": "ASIAN - Album leaf", "type": "Painting", "measurements": "Overall: 31.8 x 64.5 cm (12 1/2 x 25 3/8 in.)", "dimensions": {"overall": {"height": 0.318, "height_inch": 12, "height_inch_fraction": 0.5, "width": 0.645, "width_inch": 25, "width_inch_fraction": 0.375}}, "state_of_the_work": null, "edition_of_the_work": null, "copyright": null, "inscriptions": [{"inscription": "\u904a\u5c71\u5fd8\u6b72\u6708\uff0c\u5c50\u8204\u81ea\u76f8\u904e\u3002\n\u98a8\u9732\u5bd2\u865a\u610f\uff0c\u79aa\u6a5f\u975c\u88e1\u78e8\u3002\n\u540c\u5e74\u53e9\u68b5\u5b87\uff0c\u9042\u6b64\u8001\u7159\u863f\u3002\n\u8c48\u5411\u4eba\u9593\u8aaa\uff0c\u6797\u4e18\u81ea\u5728\u591a\u3002\n\n\u756b\u5fc5\u5e2b\u53e4\uff0c\u66f8\u4ea6\u5982\u4e4b\u3002\u89c0\u4eba\u4ea6\u7136\uff0c\u51b5\u516d\u6cd5\u4e4e\u3002\u77f3\u8c3f\u6b98\u9053\u4eba\n\u5370\u4e8c\uff1a\u77f3\u8c3f\uff0c\u767d\u79c3\u3002\u53e6\u6709\u300c\u4ecb\u4e18\u300d\u4e00\u5370\u5728\u53f3\u908a\u3002", "inscription_translation": "Artist's inscription, signature, and 3 seals:\n\nWe wandered through the mountains and forgot the time.\nOur paths crossed naturally.\nThe wind and dewdrops are cold and empty.\nAnd the Chan intuition gains its edge in silence.\nOur friends knock on the gates of my Buddhist retreat.\nTo visit the old mist-shrouded vines.\nHow can we convey to those worldly beings,\nThat life is so much more at ease in woods and hills?\n\nIn painting, one must follow the way of the ancients. Calligraphy too is like that. It is true even in character assessment, not to mention the Six Canons [of painting]. \n[2 seals] Shi xi; Bai tu. [seal, lower right edge] Jie qiu.", "inscription_remark": null, "sortorder": 1}], "exhibitions": {"current": [{"id": 516263, "title": "Fantastics and Eccentrics in Chinese Painting", "description": "<i>Fantastics and Eccentrics in Chinese Painting</i>. The Asia Society Museum, New York, NY (organizer) (March 23-May 28, 1967); Los Angeles County Museum of Art, Los Angeles, CA (June 20-August 13, 1967); Fine Arts Museums of San Francisco, de Young Museum, San Francisco, CA (September 15-November 5, 1967).", "opening_date": "1967-03-24T05:00:00"}, {"id": 301129, "title": "Year in Review: 1967", "description": "<i>Year in Review: 1967</i>. The Cleveland Museum of Art, Cleveland, OH (organizer) (November 29-December 31, 1967).", "opening_date": "1967-11-29T05:00:00"}, {"id": 304517, "title": "Eight Dynasties of Chinese Painting", "description": "<i>Eight Dynasties of Chinese Painting</i>. The Nelson-Atkins Museum of Art (November 7, 1980-January 4, 1981); The Cleveland Museum of Art (February 11-March 29, 1981); Tokyo National Museum (October 4-November 17, 1982); The Asia Society Museum, New York, NY (December 3, 1982-February 28, 1983).", "opening_date": "1981-02-11T05:00:00"}], "legacy": []}, "provenance": [{"description": "Gao Yong \u9ad8\u9095 [1850\u20131921]", "citations": [], "footnotes": null, "date": null, "sortorder": 1}, {"description": "Xu Xiaopu \u5f90\u5c0f\u5703 [1887\u20131961]", "citations": [], "footnotes": null, "date": null, "sortorder": 2}, {"description": "Walter Hochstadter [1914\u20132007], New York, NY,", "citations": [], "footnotes": null, "date": null, "sortorder": 3}, {"description": "(N. V. Hammer, Inc., New York, NY, sold to the Cleveland Museum of Art)", "citations": [], "footnotes": null, "date": "?\u20131966", "sortorder": 4}, {"description": "The Cleveland Museum of Art, Cleveland, OH", "citations": [], "footnotes": null, "date": "1966\u2013", "sortorder": 5}], "find_spot": null, "related_works": [], "former_accession_numbers": [], "did_you_know": "This spring scene was once accompanied by album leaves of summer (now in the Museum f\u00fcr Asiatiche Kunst, Berlin) and autumn and winter (now in the British Museum).", "early_education_description": null, "artlens_description": null, "description": "One of the acclaimed \"Four Monks\" (the other three being Zhu Da, Daoji, and Hongren), Kuncan was known for the rough and rustic style of his landscape paintings. This painting was once part of a large album, painted at the request of his friend Cheng Zhengkui (active 1630\u201374), with whom he shared a common interest in painting and poetry. The inscription contains a poem, which reads: <em>Wandering through mountains and oblivious of time, We met in casual shoes (and attires). The wind and dew drops harbor a chilling emptiness. Only with patience and silence can the Chan inspiration come. . . . </em>", "external_resources": {"wikidata": ["https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q60469679"], "internet_archive": ["https://archive.org/details/clevelandart-1966.367-spring-landscape"]}, "citations": [{"citation": "Tang Jisheng \u5510\u5409\u751f, and Gao Yongzhi \u9ad8\u9095\u4e4b. <em>Taishan can shi lou cang hua </em>[\u6cf0\u5c71\u6b98\u77f3\u6a13\u85cf\u756b = Painting collection of the Taishan can shi]. Shanghai: Xi leng yin she, 1926-29.", "page_number": "Portfolio 3, vol. 4, unpaginated", "url": null}, {"citation": "Cahill, James, and Virginia Field. <em>Fantastics and Eccentrics in Chinese Painting</em>. New York: Asia Society; distributed by Abrams, 1967.", "page_number": "cat. no. 20", "url": null}, {"citation": "\u201cYear in Review.\u201d <em>The Bulletin of the Cleveland Museum of Art</em> 54, no. 10 (December 1967): 302\u2013346. <br>Published as: <em>Strolling Companions in the Autumn Mountains</em>", "page_number": "Reproduced: p. 337; Mentioned: p. 346-347, no. 161", "url": "http://www.jstor.org/stable/25152183"}, {"citation": "The Cleveland Museum of Art. <em>Handbook of the Cleveland Museum of Art/1969</em>. Cleveland, OH: The Cleveland Museum of Art, 1969.", "page_number": "Reproduced: p. 268", "url": "https://archive.org/details/CMAHandbook1969/page/n292"}, {"citation": "Zhang, Wanli and Hu Renmu. <em>Badashanren shu hua ji </em>[\u516b\u5927\u5c71\u4eba\u66f8\u756b\u96c6 = Selected paintings and calligraphy of Bada Sharen]. <em>Li da ming hua jia zuo ping xuan ji </em>[\u6b77\u4ee3\u540d\u756b\u5bb6\u4f5c\u54c1\u9078\u96c6 = Selected works of famous painters in Chinese history]. Kowloon, Hong Kong: Kai fa gu fen you xian gong si, 1969.", "page_number": "Reproduced: pl. 25", "url": null}, {"citation": "Cahill, James. \"\u4e2d\u56fd\u7d75\u753b\u306b\u304a\u3051\u308b\u5947\u60f3\u3068\u5e7b\u60f3-\u4e2d.\" <em>Kokka </em>\u570b\u83ef (April 1975): pp. 5-21.", "page_number": "fig. 18", "url": null}, {"citation": "Fu, Shen \u5085\u7533. <em>Ming Qing zhi ji di ke bi gou le feng shang yu Shitao di zao qi zuo pin </em>[\u660e\u6e05\u4e4b\u969b\u7684\u6e34\u7b46\u52fe\u52d2\u98a8\u5c1a\u8207\u77f3\u6fe4\u7684\u65e9\u671f\u4f5c\u54c1 = An aspect of mid-seventeenth century Chinese painting: The \"dry linear\" style and the early work of Tao-chi]. Hong Kong: Xianggang Zhong wen da xue [\u9999\u6e2f\u4e2d\u6587\u5927\u5b78 = The Chinese University of Hong Kong], 1976.", "page_number": "p. 595", "url": null}, {"citation": "The Cleveland Museum of Art. <em>Handbook of the Cleveland Museum of Art/1978</em>. Cleveland, OH: The Cleveland Museum of Art, 1978.", "page_number": "Reproduced: p. 356", "url": "https://archive.org/details/CMAHandbook1978/page/n376"}, {"citation": "Ho, Wai-kam, Sherman E. Lee, Laurence Sickman, and Marc F. Wilson. <em>Eight Dynasties of Chinese Painting: The Collections of the Nelson Gallery-Atkins Museum, Kansas City, and the Cleveland Museum of Art</em>. Cleveland, OH: Cleveland Museum of Art, in cooperation with Indiana University Press, 1980.", "page_number": "Reproduced: cat. no. 233, pp. 315-316", "url": null}, {"citation": "Chou, Ju-hsi and Anita Chung. <em>Silent poetry: Chinese paintings from the collection of the Cleveland Museum of Art.</em> Cleveland, OH: The Cleveland Museum of Art, 2015.", "page_number": "Mentioned and Reproduced: pp. 360\u2013365", "url": null}], "url": "https://clevelandart.org/art/1966.367", "images": {"annotation": null, "web": {"url": "https://openaccess-cdn.clevelandart.org/1966.367/1966.367_web.jpg", "width": "1263", "height": "596", "filesize": "636728", "filename": "1966.367_web.jpg"}, "print": {"url": "https://openaccess-cdn.clevelandart.org/1966.367/1966.367_print.jpg", "width": "3400", "height": "1605", "filesize": "4626239", "filename": "1966.367_print.jpg"}, "full": {"url": "https://openaccess-cdn.clevelandart.org/1966.367/1966.367_full.tif", "width": "10390", "height": "4906", "filesize": "203921888", "filename": "1966.367_full.tif"}}, "alternate_images": [{"web": {"url": "https://openaccess-cdn.clevelandart.org/1966.367/1966.367_alt0_web.jpg", "width": "1109", "height": "893", "filesize": "862811"}, "print": {"url": "https://openaccess-cdn.clevelandart.org/1966.367/1966.367_alt0_print.jpg", "width": "3400", "height": "2738", "filesize": "8812628"}, "full": {"url": "https://openaccess-cdn.clevelandart.org/1966.367/1966.367_alt0_full.tif", "width": "6197", "height": "4992", "filesize": "92838072"}, "date_created": "2010-05-19T19:05:27", "annotation": ""}, {"web": {"url": "https://openaccess-cdn.clevelandart.org/1966.367/1966.367_alt1_web.jpg", "width": "1193", "height": "893", "filesize": "855800"}, "print": {"url": "https://openaccess-cdn.clevelandart.org/1966.367/1966.367_alt1_print.jpg", "width": "3400", "height": "2545", "filesize": "7706999"}, "full": {"url": "https://openaccess-cdn.clevelandart.org/1966.367/1966.367_alt1_full.tif", "width": "6668", "height": "4992", "filesize": "99890100"}, "date_created": "2010-05-19T19:09:40", "annotation": ""}, {"web": {"url": "https://openaccess-cdn.clevelandart.org/1966.367/1966.367_alt2_web.jpg", "width": "1193", "height": "893", "filesize": "887156"}, "print": {"url": "https://openaccess-cdn.clevelandart.org/1966.367/1966.367_alt2_print.jpg", "width": "3400", "height": "2545", "filesize": "8078488"}, "full": {"url": "https://openaccess-cdn.clevelandart.org/1966.367/1966.367_alt2_full.tif", "width": "6668", "height": "4992", "filesize": "99888172"}, "date_created": "2010-05-19T19:13:45", "annotation": ""}, {"web": {"url": "https://openaccess-cdn.clevelandart.org/1966.367/1966.367_alt3_web.jpg", "width": "1263", "height": "630", "filesize": "606743"}, "print": {"url": "https://openaccess-cdn.clevelandart.org/1966.367/1966.367_alt3_print.jpg", "width": "3400", "height": "1695", "filesize": "3942270"}, "full": {"url": "https://openaccess-cdn.clevelandart.org/1966.367/1966.367_alt3_full.tif", "width": "6000", "height": "2992", "filesize": "53876568"}, "date_created": "2004-02-19T20:00:24", "annotation": ""}], "creditline": "Purchase from the J. H. Wade Fund", "image_credit": null, "sketchfab_id": null, "sketchfab_url": null, "gallery_donor_text": null, "athena_id": 142642, "creators": [{"id": 31221, "description": "Kuncan (Chinese, 1612\u2013c. 1673)", "extent": null, "qualifier": null, "role": "artist", "biography": "Kuncan was one of the so-called Four Monks of the early Qing period.", "name_in_original_language": "\u9ae0\u6b98", "birth_year": "1612", "death_year": "1678", "use_in_caption": true, "include_extent": false, "weight": 1}], "legal_status": "accessioned", "accession_date": "1966-11-05T00:00:00", "sortable_date": 1666, "date_added_to_oa": null, "date_text": "1666", "collapse_artists": false, "on_loan": false, "recently_acquired": false, "record_type": "object", "conservation_statement": null, "has_conservation_images": false, "cover_accession_number": null, "is_nazi_era_provenance": false, "impression": null, "alternate_titles": ["Wandering Through the Mountains and Forgetting the Years", "Spring Landscape \u6625\u666f\u5716", "Strolling Companions in the Autumn Mountains"], "is_highlight": false, "updated_at": "2026-09-04 11:08:46.208000"}, {"id": 132908, "accession_number": "1955.36", "share_license_status": "CC0", "tombstone": "Landscape after Guo Zhongshu (\u4eff\u90ed\u5fe0\u6055\u5c71\u6c34), c. 1680\u20131705. Bada Shanren (Chinese, 1626\u20131705). Hanging scroll; ink on paper; painting: 109.9 x 56.4 cm (43 1/4 x 22 3/16 in.); overall with knobs: 247.7 x 84.5 cm (97 1/2 x 33 1/4 in.). The Cleveland Museum of Art, John L. Severance Fund, 1955.36", "current_location": null, "title": "Landscape after Guo Zhongshu", "title_in_original_language": "\u4eff\u90ed\u5fe0\u6055\u5c71\u6c34", "creation_date": "c. 1680\u20131705", "creation_date_earliest": 1675, "creation_date_latest": 1705, "artists_tags": ["male"], "culture": ["China, Qing dynasty (1644\u20131911)"], "technique": "Hanging scroll; ink on paper", "support_materials": [], "department": "Chinese Art", "collection": "ASIAN - Hanging scroll", "type": "Painting", "measurements": "Painting: 109.9 x 56.4 cm (43 1/4 x 22 3/16 in.); Overall with knobs: 247.7 x 84.5 cm (97 1/2 x 33 1/4 in.)", "dimensions": {"painting": {"height": 1.099, "height_inch": 43, "height_inch_fraction": 0.25, "width": 0.564, "width_inch": 22, "width_inch_fraction": 0.1875}, "overall with knobs": {"height": 2.477, "height_inch": 97, "height_inch_fraction": 0.5, "width": 0.845, "width_inch": 33, "width_inch_fraction": 0.25}, "overall": {"height": 2.477, "height_inch": 97, "height_inch_fraction": 0.5, "width": 0.74, "width_inch": 29, "width_inch_fraction": 0.125}}, "state_of_the_work": null, "edition_of_the_work": null, "copyright": null, "inscriptions": [{"inscription": "Artist's inscription, signature, and 3 seals: Painting after Guo Shuxian [Guo Zhongshu]. Bada shanren. [2 seals] Shanren; Kede shenxian \u53ef\u5f97\u795e\u4ed9. [seal, lower left corner] Yaozhu \u9065\u5c5e", "inscription_translation": null, "inscription_remark": null, "sortorder": 1}, {"inscription": "8 additional seals: 1 of Li Shifen (1821\u20131885); 4 of Chang Y\u00fcan \u5f35\u7230 [Zhang Daqian \u5f35\u5927\u5343] (1899\u20131983); 3 unidentified.", "inscription_translation": null, "inscription_remark": null, "sortorder": 2}], "exhibitions": {"current": [{"id": 300427, "title": "Chinese Landscape Painting", "description": "<i>Chinese Landscape Painting</i>. The Cleveland Museum of Art, Cleveland, OH (organizer) (November 5-December 26, 1954).", "opening_date": "1954-11-05T04:00:00"}, {"id": 300857, "title": "Art: The International Language", "description": "<i>Art: The International Language</i>. The Cleveland Museum of Art (October 2-November 4, 1956).", "opening_date": "1956-10-02T04:00:00"}, {"id": 520794, "title": "Fifteen Chinese Paintings from the Cleveland Museum of Art", "description": "<i>Fifteen Chinese Paintings from the Cleveland Museum of Art</i>. Smith College Museum of Art, Northampton, MA (organizer) (October 9-28, 1964).", "opening_date": "1964-10-09T04:00:00"}, {"id": 444960, "title": "Chu Ta: Selected Paintings and Calligraphy", "description": "<i>Chu Ta: Selected Paintings and Calligraphy</i>. The Frances Lehman Loeb Art Center (organizer) (December 2, 1972-January 28, 1973); The New York Cultural Center, New York, NY (February 28-April 15, 1973).", "opening_date": "1972-12-02T05:00:00"}, {"id": 310041, "title": "Mountains, Rocks, and Water: Landscape Painting in Asia", "description": "<i>Mountains, Rocks, and Water: Landscape Painting in Asia</i>. The Cleveland Museum of Art, Cleveland, OH (organizer) (October 2-December 13, 1987).", "opening_date": "1987-10-02T04:00:00"}, {"id": 666887, "title": "The Dancing Brush: Ming Dynasty Calligraphers and Eccentrics", "description": "<i>The Dancing Brush: Ming Dynasty Calligraphers and Eccentrics</i>. The Cleveland Museum of Art, Cleveland, OH (organizer) (September 8, 2024-March 2, 2025).", "opening_date": "2024-09-08T04:00:00"}], "legacy": [{"description": "<em>Eight Dynasties of Chinese Painting</em>. The Nelson-Atkins Museum of Art (November 7, 1980-January 4, 1981); The Cleveland Museum of Art (February 10-March 29, 1981); Tokyo National Museum (October 4-November 17, 1982).", "opening_date": "1981-02-10T00:00:00"}, {"description": "<em>Main Asian Rotation (Gallery 242)</em>. The Cleveland Museum of Art, Cleveland, OH (November 21, 2013-July 28, 2014).", "opening_date": "2013-11-21T00:00:00"}]}, "provenance": [{"description": "Chang Dai-chien [Zhang Daqian \u5f35\u5927\u5343] [1899\u20131983]", "citations": [], "footnotes": null, "date": null, "sortorder": 1}, {"description": "(Walter Hochstadter [1914\u20132007], New York, NY,  sold to the Cleveland Museum of Art)", "citations": [], "footnotes": null, "date": "?\u20131955", "sortorder": 2}, {"description": "The Cleveland Museum of Art, Cleveland, OH", "citations": [], "footnotes": null, "date": "1955\u2013", "sortorder": 3}], "find_spot": null, "related_works": [], "former_accession_numbers": [], "did_you_know": "Zhu Da's inscription acknowledges that this painting was done after the early Song master Guo Zhongshu \u90ed\u5fe0\u6055, but there is almost no tangible stylistic relation to be found between Zhu Da and his 10th-century model.", "early_education_description": null, "artlens_description": null, "description": "Similar to some calligraphers of his time, Zhu Da rejected conventions in favor of an individual, personal expression. He is known for ambiguous compositions of fish, flowers, birds, and rocks in contrasting ink tonality. As a member of the Ming imperial family, Zhu lost his princely status and hid in a monastery when the Manchus, foreigners from the north, established the Qing dynasty in 1644.<br><br>In this late work, mountain ranges are rendered in diverse and dense strokes rising toward the top of the scroll. It references the artist Dong Qichang (1555\u20131636) in concept. Yet the cursory brushwork and composition present Zhu\u2019s personal style.", "external_resources": {"wikidata": ["https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q60516766"], "internet_archive": ["https://archive.org/details/clevelandart-1955.36-landscape-after-guo"]}, "citations": [{"citation": "Zhang, Daqian \u5f35\u5927\u5343. <em>Da feng tang shu hua lu</em> \u5927\u98a8\u5802\u66f8\u756b\u9304. Chengdu: [publisher not identified], 1943.", "page_number": "p. 42(b)", "url": null}, {"citation": "Lee, Sherman E. <em>Chinese Landscape Painting</em>. Cleveland, OH: Cleveland Museum of Art, 1954.", "page_number": "Reproduced: cat. no. 98", "url": null}, {"citation": "Sire\u0301n, Osvald. <em>Chinese Painting: Leading Masters and Principles</em>. New York: Ronald Press, 1956.", "page_number": "Mentioned and Reproduced: V, 154; VII, Lists, 325", "url": null}, {"citation": "Lee, Sherman E. \u201cThe Two Styles of Chu Ta.\u201d <em>The Bulletin of the Cleveland Museum of Art</em>, vol. 45, no. 9, 1958, pp. 215\u2013219.", "page_number": "Mentioned: pp. 218, 219; Reproduced: p. 210", "url": "www.jstor.org/stable/25142297"}, {"citation": "Grousset, Rene\u0301. <em>Chinese Art &amp; Culture</em>. London: A. Deutsch, 1959.", "page_number": "Reproduced: pl. 58", "url": null}, {"citation": "Lee, Sherman E. <em>Chinese Landscape Painting</em>. Cleveland, OH: The Cleveland Museum of Art, 1962.", "page_number": "Mentioned: p. 116, no. 92", "url": null}, 