 22.3 x 9.6 cm (6 x 8 3/4 x 3 3/4 in.). The Cleveland Museum of Art, Worcester R. Warner Collection, 1917.25", "current_location": null, "title": "Landscape", "title_in_original_language": "\u77f3\u96d5\u5c71\u6c34\u4eba\u7269\u5c71\u5b50", "creation_date": "1644\u20131911", "creation_date_earliest": 1644, "creation_date_latest": 1911, "artists_tags": [], "culture": ["China, Qing dynasty (1644-1911)"], "technique": "soapstone", "support_materials": [], "department": "Chinese Art", "collection": "China - Qing Dynasty", "type": "Stone", "measurements": "Overall: 15.3 x 22.3 x 9.6 cm (6 x 8 3/4 x 3 3/4 in.)", "dimensions": {"overall": {"height": 0.153, "height_inch": 6, "height_inch_fraction": 0.0, "width": 0.223, "width_inch": 8, "width_inch_fraction": 0.75, "depth": 0.096, "depth_inch": 3, "depth_inch_fraction": 0.75}}, "state_of_the_work": null, "edition_of_the_work": null, "copyright": null, "inscriptions": [{"inscription": "\u77f3\u9580\u6d1e\u5929", "inscription_translation": "Stonegate Cave to Heaven (\"shimen dongtian\")", "inscription_remark": null, "sortorder": null}], "exhibitions": {"current": [{"id": 287904, "title": "Chaekgeori: Pleasure of Possessions in Korean Painted Screens", "description": "<i>Chaekgeori: Pleasure of Possessions in Korean Painted Screens</i>. The Cleveland Museum of Art, Cleveland, OH (August 5-November 5, 2017).", "opening_date": "2017-08-05T04:00:00"}, {"id": 448467, "title": "China through the Magnifying Glass: Masterpieces in Miniature and Detail", "description": "<i>China through the Magnifying Glass: Masterpieces in Miniature and Detail</i>. The Cleveland Museum of Art, Cleveland, OH (organizer) (December 11, 2022-February 26, 2023).", "opening_date": "2022-12-10T05:00:00"}], "legacy": []}, "provenance": [{"description": "Worcester R. Warner [1846\u20131929], Cleveland, OH, given to the Cleveland Museum of Art", "citations": [], "footnotes": null, "date": "?\u20131917", "sortorder": 1}, {"description": "The Cleveland Museum of Art, Cleveland, OH", "citations": [], "footnotes": null, "date": "1917\u2013", "sortorder": 2}], "find_spot": null, "related_works": [], "former_accession_numbers": ["1662.1916"], "did_you_know": "A waterfall plummets down the cliff by the temple and then flows smoothly down to join the river at the front of the landscape scene.", "early_education_description": null, "artlens_description": null, "description": "A mountain scenery surrounded by water and fish is meticulously carved out of soapstone, with a pond, bridge, waterfall, and temple front in its center. The unidentified figure scene on the left includes an ox and a man wearing what appears to be a Korean hat. A Buddha figure hidden in the depth of the temple can be glimpsed from the backside. The inscribed pillar on the right reads \u201cStonegate Cave to Heaven (<em>shimen dongtian</em>)\u201d. Indentations all over the stone suggest that the miniature mountain was once adorned with precious stones and metal, presumably representing an earthly paradise to which one could escape in one\u2019s mind and imagination.", "external_resources": {"wikidata": ["https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q79482144"], "internet_archive": ["https://archive.org/details/clevelandart-1917.25-landscape"]}, "citations": [], "url": "https://clevelandart.org/art/1917.25", "images": {"annotation": null, "web": {"url": "https://openaccess-cdn.clevelandart.org/1917.25/1917.25_web.jpg", "width": "900", "height": "645", "filesize": "179741", "filename": "1917.25_web.jpg"}, "print": {"url": "https://openaccess-cdn.clevelandart.org/1917.25/1917.25_print.jpg", "width": "3400", "height": "2435", "filesize": "1711467", "filename": "1917.25_print.jpg"}, "full": {"url": "https://openaccess-cdn.clevelandart.org/1917.25/1917.25_full.tif", "width": "7798", "height": "5584", "filesize": "130661740", "filename": "1917.25_full.tif"}}, "alternate_images": [{"web": {"url": "https://openaccess-cdn.clevelandart.org/1917.25/1917.25_alt0_web.jpg", "width": "900",